cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Layercake — a place, its layers, its years"
message: "If you use Layercake or a study built with it, please cite it as below, and cite each data source as its licence asks."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Ozvåag LLC"
  - family-names: Oswood
    given-names: Carter
repository-code: "https://github.com/ozvaag/layercake"
url: "https://layercake.pages.dev"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
abstract: >-
  An open engine and study format for reading geographic factors against each
  other over time: a physical frame (relief, drainage, basins), a gridded field
  (reanalysis climate), marks on places (regional statistics), dated instruments
  with a scope (law, plans, infrastructure) and national series, on one sheet
  and one year axis, with every figure carrying its source. Studies are
  reproducible folders built by one command from open, keyless sources.
keywords: [geography, climate, policy, agriculture, public-health, reproducible-research, atlas]
